schema: "0.4"
id: "fim-audio-and-sound-tone_js-01-synth-composition"
type: audio
quality: high
solution: tone_js
category: audio-and-sound
variant: synth-composition
references:
  - "references/fim/overview/music-audio-ml/tone_js.md"
  - "references/fim/solution/tone_js.md"
prompt:
  system: |-
    Generate production-quality Tone.js browser audio assets for FIM evaluation. Output only the requested source artifact, with no markdown fences or explanatory prose.
  text: |-
    Create a self-contained Tone.js synth composition artifact for the audio-and-sound category.

    Scenario:
    Build a short generative browser composition that demonstrates musical structure: tempo, meter, melodic motifs, chords, bass movement, percussion, effects, and a visual transport status panel. The piece must begin only after a user gesture and must be suitable for repeated start, stop, reset, and dispose cycles in a single-page app.

    Implementation requirements:
    - Use Tone.js 15 from a CDN or an equivalent import pattern.
    - Provide an explicit Enable Audio or Play button that calls await Tone.start() before any sound.
    - Use Tone.Transport for tempo, time signature, loop points, and scheduled playback; do not drive musical timing with setTimeout or setInterval.
    - Use at least three musical sources, such as PolySynth, FMSynth, MembraneSynth, NoiseSynth, MonoSynth, or Sampler with a loading fallback.
    - Use Tone.Sequence, Tone.Part, Tone.Loop, or Tone.Pattern so every callback passes the provided time argument into triggerAttackRelease.
    - Include gain staging with a master Tone.Gain or Tone.Channel, conservative levels, a limiter or compressor, and no clipping-prone destination chain.
    - Shape attacks and releases to avoid clicks, and include effect routing with wet/dry control for delay, reverb, chorus, filter, or EQ.
    - Include cleanup and dispose behavior for every synth, effect, sequence, part, loop, analyser, and transport state created by the artifact.
    - Include visible state for stopped, starting, playing, muted, unsupported Web Audio, and sample-load failure if samples are used.
    - Include accessible controls with labels, keyboard operation, muted default option, and a short text summary of what the audio represents.
    - Output only a complete HTML document with inline CSS and JavaScript.
  requirements:
    - "Autoplay policy: Tone.start() is called only inside a click, tap, or keyboard activation handler."
    - "Timing: all musical events are scheduled with Tone.Transport and Tone callback time values."
    - "Gain staging: master level, effect wet levels, and dynamics processing prevent clipping."
    - "Cleanup/dispose: stop, cancel, and dispose Tone nodes and scheduled events on reset, destroy, and page unload."
    - "Fallback checks: show clear UI when Web Audio, CDN loading, sample loading, or audio unlock fails."
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
output:
  text_format: html
  artifact: "Tone.js synth composition browser audio source"
  formats:
    - format: html
    - format: js
  render_expectation: "Interactive browser audio that plays only after user activation and can be captured through audio output or inspected through visible transport diagnostics."
evaluation:
  checklist:
    - "YAML parses under schema 0.4, all required fields are present, and all file text is ASCII-only."
    - "Generated artifact is a complete Tone.js HTML or JavaScript browser asset with no markdown fences."
    - "Composition uses Tone.Transport plus Tone.Sequence, Tone.Part, Tone.Loop, or Tone.Pattern for musical timing."
    - "Autoplay policy is respected with await Tone.start() inside a user gesture before sound starts."
    - "Gain staging includes a master gain or channel, conservative source levels, ramps or envelopes, and clipping protection."
    - "Audio structure includes melody, harmony or bass, percussion or pulse, and at least one effect chain."
    - "Timing uses scheduled callback time values and does not rely on JavaScript timers for rhythm."
    - "Cleanup/dispose stops transport, clears scheduled events, and disposes all created Tone nodes and event objects."
    - "Fallback checks cover unsupported Web Audio, failed CDN import, sample loading if used, and muted or suspended state."
  rubric:
    - name: "Format validity"
      weight: 30
      criteria: "YAML parses, schema 0.4 fields are present, generated output is valid HTML or JavaScript, and file name, id, solution, category, type, and variant align."
    - name: "Semantic completeness"
      weight: 30
      criteria: "The artifact fulfills the synth composition scenario and uses Tone.js Transport, sources, scheduling, effects, autoplay unlock, and disposal patterns from the references."
    - name: "Audio/structural quality"
      weight: 25
      criteria: "The composition has coherent musical layers, stable timing, readable state, clean envelopes, intentional timbre, useful effects, and no obvious clipping."
    - name: "Robustness"
      weight: 15
      criteria: "The artifact handles browser autoplay, unsupported audio, load failure, repeated start/stop, cleanup, responsive UI, and accessibility states without runtime failure."
  pass_conditions:
    - "Rubric weights sum to 100 with Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, Audio/structural quality 25, and Robustness 15."
    - "Score is at least 80 out of 100."
    - "No critical failure in YAML parsing, Tone.js loading, autoplay unlock, gain staging, timing, cleanup/dispose, or fallback checks."
    - "Generated content is clearly aligned with Tone.js and does not substitute raw Web Audio except through Tone.js internals or a documented fallback."
tags:
  - "fim"
  - "audio-and-sound"
  - "tone_js"
  - "synth-composition"
  - "tone-transport"
  - "sequencing"
  - "browser-audio"
